    "body": "Hmm, this seems reasonable to me. It's a bit awkward since now there's sentences\n\n>  The data to be sent is the data stored in the section of the buffer described by the ArrayBuffer object that data references.\n\nand\n\n> ... must increase the bufferedAmount attribute by the length of data's buffer in bytes\n\nwhich is a bit weird when the argument _is_ an ArrayBuffer, but the phrasing still kind of works. WDYT, @annevk?\n",
